audio machine_dlkm (lahaina.c): ACK 6.18 removed android_vh_snd_pcm_check_no_buffer

<trace/hooks/sound.h> is gone. On 6.12 lahaina.c's hook handler let snd_pcm_pre_start()
start the PLAYBACK side of the hostless FE links (VoiceMMode1/2, LSM1-7, "Secondary MI2S_TX
Hostless Capture") with an empty host buffer (5.4: substream->hw_no_buffer). Without it, a
voice call's playback FE START would fail with -EPIPE unless userspace sets stop_threshold
to the boundary itself.

6.18 equivalent, inside the module: those links get a dai_link .prepare op (they had none;
a link with its own ops is reported and left alone). Prepare runs after hw_params/sw_params,
right before START, and sets the PLAYBACK stop_threshold to the boundary, which makes
snd_pcm_playback_data() true for the empty buffer. Same link test as 6.12
(qcom_link_is_hostless()); capture is unaffected, as it was on 6.12.

